codemasters the developer of dirt grid  and the f1 series of racing games has  hired developers from evolution studios  the team behind playstation 4 racing sim  driveclub writing on its blog the  publisher said codemasters will be  expanding its portfolio of studios to  include the highly respected and very  talented team from evolution studios on  my 22nd sony announced plans to close  evolution meaning that many of the  studio's work for space redundancy  according to codemasters the success of  F 1 2015 and dirt rally has repositioned  the company for growth which starts the  acquisition of talent from the formerly  PlayStation exclusive development studio  the expansion will not only CS gained a  wealth of racing expertise and skill but  it'll take code masses to the next level  as the world's largest racing focused  game company with phenomenal racing DNA  we hope the gamers out there excited to  see what we do next as are all the rest  of us at codys evolution studios  co-founder Mick Hawking has been  appointed vp of product development at  codemasters he'll be responsible for all  the company studios including the  addition of nav multi-platform evolution  team I am delighted to be joining  codemasters at such an exciting time in  the company's growth he said we have  shared a passion for racing a desire to  innovate and a determination to create  the best racing games and build the best  racing community in the market I'm very  much looking forward to working with so  many of the world's greatest racing  developers on new IP as well as existing  franchises including dirt grid Micro  Machines and the Formula One games in  his previous statement announcing the  closure of evolution sony said that the  restructure would allow it to focus on  other studios that already have exciting  new projects in development it continued  we believe will be in a stronger  position going forward and able to offer  the best possible content of the highest  quality for our consumers at the time  poorest in ski directory of driveclub  banked fans and Sony for their support  firstly a big thank you to all the fans  have supported us through evo storied  history we couldn't have helped achieve  what we did without you thank you to  Sony who helped Eva rise the top tier of  racing game teams in the world working  as a first-party team has been a  fantastic experience so are you excited  to see what this new team can build  together let us know in the comments  section below or find me on twitter at  arregle dave and for your gaming news  stay tuned to gamespot com  you
 

